{
	"$comment": "THE shared money oracle for the order write contract. One truth for the client's divergence comparator and for the plugin-side write-contract tests, so both sides argue against the same arithmetic instead of two hand-typed copies. Scenario: 3 x 9.99 ex-tax, GB 20% VAT plus a 2% COMPOUND surcharge, store display decimals 2, taxes rounded at subtotal. `pos` is MEASURED from packages/order-math (calculateOrderTotals), not hand-derived — which is why it is not six decimals throughout: WooCommerce stores money per field and order-math mirrors it field for field. `server6dp` is the same order as the plugin serves it since woocommerce-pos#1466 (dp=6 on every WCPOS order surface); note that order-level `total` and `total_tax` are 2dp VALUES merely padded to a six-decimal STRING, because WC_Abstract_Order stores them at display decimals on every route. `server2dp` is the legacy shape from before that fix, retained so version skew stays pinned. A comparator that flags `pos` against either server shape is over-strict; one that flags nothing at all is useless. See packages/sync-engine/src/write-path/order-money-divergence.ts.",
